
To run this program, you'll need:
 - Python (at least version 3)
 - ACME (at least version 0.97)


To be able to run this program from any directory, you need to include
it in your search path:

For example, if you have checked out this repository to
	/home/USERNAME/githubrepos/mca2
then enter this to add the start program to the search path:

	cd
	mkdir bin	(..."already exists" errors can be ignored)
	cd bin
	ln -s ../githubrepos/mca2/mca2.py .

now logout, and when you login again, "mca2.py" should be available
whenever you open a terminal.
